  "title": "SparrKULee: A Speech-Evoked Auditory Response Repository from KU Leuven, Containing the EEG of 85 Participants",
  "description": "SparrKULee is a speech-evoked auditory response repository from KU Leuven containing EEG recorded from normal-hearing native Dutch/Flemish speakers listening to continuous speech. This NEMAR re-host includes 80 of the original 85 participants across 11 session types (shortstories01 and varyingStories01-10), plus resting-state recordings. The data support research on neural tracking of speech and auditory EEG decoding.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with a BioSemi ActiveTwo system, with raw data stored as BDF files, while participants listened to continuous speech stimuli (short stories) in active listening sessions. Participants were 18-30 years old with normal hearing (≤30 dB HL). Recordings are aligned to stimuli via triggers, and the dataset includes resting-state recordings.",
  "license": "Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International License (CC BY-NC 4.0) for the EEG data. Stimuli can only be used for non-commercial purposes.",
